                  "rawKnowledgeId": "raw_knowledge_1",
                  "rawKnowledge": "When a file's name already exists in the destination, the existing file is quietly replaced. The row ends up updated rather than created. Re-uploading `report.pdf` overwrites the existing one without asking. Work is in progress to replace this with a prompt (\"Replace\", \"Keep both\", or \"Cancel\") plus an automatic-rename option. The rename logic has a known rough edge: because it bumps a trailing number, a photo named `IMG_4521.jpg` would become `IMG_4522.jpg` (likely the next photo's name) instead of something safe like `IMG_4521 (1).jpg`.",
                  "whyPotentiallyRelevant": "The user's issue with renaming files in Twake Drive may be related to the current behavior of file name clashes and the upcoming UI update for renaming options. The known issue describes the current behavior of silently replacing files with the same name and the upcoming changes to the rename logic.",
